# Fire a Wand of Cleansing Light at an aberration and let the screen say what
# the wand rolled. Read by tools/check_wand_cleansing.sh, finding PA-08-F1 of
# bd inc-tek.8.8.
#
# The run needs one wand of a KNOWN plus and one target the wand will accept,
# and it must reach both without a monster writing over the window the damage
# is printed in. So, in order:
#
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu. Later
#                            entries need 'w' alone; the 'y' answers the
#                            one-time "enter wizard mode?" question.
#   Wizard Mode Switches     DOWN*10 walks to Freeze Monsters, the 11th row
#   DOWN*10 SPACE ESC        (src/Tables.cpp:2610-2656). SPACE toggles and does
#                            not move the cursor. Frozen monsters do not walk
#                            up and attack while the wand is being fetched.
#   Item Acquisition         RIGHT*4 walks the glyph row to Wands: ItemGlyphs
#   RIGHT*4                  (src/Tables.cpp:320) puts -AI_WAND 4 steps along,
#                            and the header line names the category.
#   @until "Wand of Soul     the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#     Flaying" DOWN          cursor is walked. Three rows show and the MIDDLE
#                            one is selected, so the run stops on the pass
#                            where the row BELOW the wanted one appears. Soul
#                            Flaying is the entry after Cleansing Light in
#                            lib/m_items.irh. That is an ordering assumption,
#                            and the check does not trust it: it reads the
#                            wand's name back off the screen before believing
#                            anything.
#   ENTER 2 ENTER            take it. "Enter Item Level:" sets the item's plus
#                            (src/Debug.cpp:613-622 calls SetInherentPlus with
#                            what is typed), so the wand is a known +2 and both
#                            numbers the check compares are predictable.
#   s ESC                    stow it in the pack and close the manager. The
#                            manager refuses to close with an item in the air.
#   Monster Summoning        an aether sponge, the first aberration on the
#   a a RIGHT ENTER          list, placed one square east. It must be an
#                            aberration, undead or outsider: EV_ISTARGET
#                            (lib/m_items.irh) refuses everything else, which
#                            is why the player himself is an "[Invalid
#                            Target]". It must also be something that does not
#                            act: an umber hulk gazes on the same turn and its
#                            own damage line overwrites the wand's.
#   b a RIGHT                blast, choose the wand, fire east.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*4
@until "Wand of Soul Flaying" DOWN
ENTER
2
ENTER
@dump:wand-in-hand
s
ESC
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
a
a
RIGHT
ENTER
b
a
RIGHT
@dump:fired
